From: Holodor <holodor@bonesaw.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:42:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] usb: core: hub: preserve default autosuspend delay on HUB_QUIRK_CHECK_PORT_AUTOSUSPEND

Genesys Logic USB 2.1 hubs (05e3:0610, commonly used in USB-C HDMI/Ethernet
docks) take ~200 ms after hub_power_on() to check downstream ports before
reporting port connect status. Setting autosuspend_delay to 0 in hub_probe()
causes the hub to runtime-suspend 125 ms after hub_power_on(), resulting in an
infinite 0.83s resume -> port connect -> reset loop.

Keep the default 2000 ms autosuspend_delay on hubs carrying
HUB_QUIRK_CHECK_PORT_AUTOSUSPEND in id->driver_info.

Signed-off-by: Holodor <holodor@bonesaw.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/core/hub.c b/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
--- a/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
@@ -1919,7 +1919,8 @@
 	 *   usbcore.autosuspend = -1 then keep autosuspend disabled.
 	 */
 #ifdef CONFIG_PM
-	if (hdev->dev.power.autosuspend_delay >= 0)
+	if (hdev->dev.power.autosuspend_delay >= 0 &&
+	    !(id->driver_info & HUB_QUIRK_CHECK_PORT_AUTOSUSPEND))
 		pm_runtime_set_autosuspend_delay(&hdev->dev, 0);
 #endif
 
